meta {
  name: 6 Answer a reschedule request
  type: http
  seq: 6
}
post {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/booking/appointments/{{appointmentIdentifier}}/reschedule-answer
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "approve": true
  }
}
docs {
  Approving or declining an outstanding proposal. One route with a bool rather than two, because both
  answers share every precondition — same appointment, same authorisation, same "is there still
  something to answer" — and differ only in the write.

  ⚠️ **The answer must come from the OTHER party.** Answering your own proposal returns `409`
  ("The other party has to answer a reschedule request, not the one who made it") — otherwise asking
  and agreeing would be one act, and a customer could move a provider's session unilaterally. So run
  this as whichever side did NOT send request #5.

  `approve: true` — the session moves to `proposedStart`, its LENGTH is preserved, `previousStart` is
  recorded, the proposal is cleared and the status returns to `1` (`Booked`).

  `approve: false` — the session stays exactly where it was, the proposal is cleared, status returns to
  `Booked`, and `previousStart` stays **null**: a declined proposal must not read afterwards as though a
  reschedule happened.

  Either way the proposer is notified. Declining is news too — silence reads as an unanswered request.
}
